/*!
\page qt-apple-cmake-opt-outs.html
\title Apple Platform CMake Opt-outs
\brief Variables and properties that turn off Qt's defaults on Apple platforms.

When \l qt_finalize_target() finalizes an application bundle on macOS, iOS,
or visionOS, Qt sets several target properties, Info.plist values, and Xcode
attributes to sensible defaults. Most defaults are skipped when the project
already provides a value, either through the target property or through the
matching \c{CMAKE_XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_<name>} variable. The exceptions are:

\list
\li The bundle name and version defaults check the matching
    \c{MACOSX_BUNDLE_*} target properties and variables instead.
\li The bundle identifier default reuses an identifier that the project sets
    through \c MACOSX_BUNDLE_GUI_IDENTIFIER or
    \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER, and sets both properties.
\li The localization defaults overwrite an existing
    \c CFBundleDevelopmentRegion in Info.plist.
\endlist

Each default can also be turned off with one of the variables described on
this page.

Set the variables to \c TRUE before the target is finalized, for example on the
command line or in the project's top-level \c CMakeLists.txt.

\section1 Xcode Attributes

These defaults are only applied when using the Xcode generator.

\table
\header \li Variable \li Effect when set
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM_ID
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM from the first team
         found on the system. See \l QT_NO_SET_XCODE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM_ID.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_CODE_SIGN_STYLE
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_CODE_SIGN_STYLE to \c Automatic.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_INSTALL_PATH
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_INSTALL_PATH to \c{$(inherited)}.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT per
         configuration (\c dwarf for Debug, \c dwarf-with-dsym otherwise).
         Only a value of the property without a \c{[variant=<config>]}
         suffix counts as provided by the project.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_GCC_GENERATE_DEBUGGING_SYMBOLS
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_GCC_GENERATE_DEBUGGING_SYMBOLS to
         \c YES.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_COPY_PHASE_STRIP
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_COPY_PHASE_STRIP to \c NO. Without the
         default, Xcode strips embedded frameworks, such as the Qt
         frameworks, when copying them into the app bundle.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_MARKETING_VERSION and
         \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
     \li Do not set the \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_MARKETING_VERSION and
         \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION properties. Setting either
         of the two variables turns off both properties. Info.plist then gets
         literal version strings instead of Xcode build setting references.
\endtable

\section1 iOS Attributes

These defaults are applied on iOS only.

\table
\header \li Variable \li Effect when set
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY to iPhone and
         iPad (\c{1,2}).
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_ENABLE_BITCODE
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_ENABLE_BITCODE to \c NO.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_ARCHS
     \li Do not restrict the iOS simulator to \c x86_64 when Qt was built with
         that architecture.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_LD_ENTRY_POINT
     \li Do not set \c XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_LD_ENTRY_POINT to Qt's main wrapper.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_DEFAULT_IOS_LAUNCH_SCREEN
     \li Do not use Qt's default launch screen storyboard when the project
         provides none. See
         \l{cmake-variable-QT_IOS_LAUNCH_SCREEN}{QT_IOS_LAUNCH_SCREEN}. The
         target property of the same name takes precedence over the variable.
\row \li \c QT_NO_ADD_IOS_LAUNCH_SCREEN_TO_BUNDLE
     \li Do not add the launch screen storyboard to the app bundle.
\endtable

\section1 Bundle Metadata

These defaults are applied on all Apple platforms and with all generators.

\table
\header \li Variable \li Effect when set
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER
     \li Do not set the bundle identifier properties. See
         \l QT_NO_SET_XCODE_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_BUNDLE_NAME
     \li Do not set \c MACOSX_BUNDLE_BUNDLE_NAME.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_XCODE_BUNDLE_VERSION
     \li Do not set placeholder values for \c MACOSX_BUNDLE_BUNDLE_VERSION and
         \c MACOSX_BUNDLE_SHORT_VERSION_STRING.
\row \li \c QT_NO_SET_PLIST_LOCALIZATIONS
     \li Do not write \c CFBundleDevelopmentRegion and \c CFBundleLocalizations
         into Info.plist.
\endtable

\section1 Shared Library Embedding

The \l{apple-embed-shared-library-dependencies}{embedding of shared libraries}
into application bundles is controlled by target properties:

\list
\li \l{cmake-target-property-QT_NO_XCODE_EMBED_FRAMEWORKS}
    {QT_NO_XCODE_EMBED_FRAMEWORKS} turns it off for an application.
\li \l{cmake-target-property-QT_NO_XCODE_EMBED_FRAMEWORK_IN_CONSUMERS}
    {QT_NO_XCODE_EMBED_FRAMEWORK_IN_CONSUMERS} leaves out a single library.
\endlist

\section1 SDK and Xcode Version Checks

These variables affect the SDK and Xcode version checks that run when
configuring Qt itself.

\table
\header \li Variable \li Effect when set
\row \li \c QT_NO_APPLE_SDK_AND_XCODE_CHECK
     \li Skip all SDK and Xcode version checks.
\row \li \c QT_NO_APPLE_SDK_MIN_VERSION_CHECK
     \li Skip the minimum SDK version check.
\row \li \c QT_NO_XCODE_MIN_VERSION_CHECK
     \li Skip the minimum Xcode version check, and do not require Xcode to be
         installed.
\row \li \c QT_NO_APPLE_SDK_MAX_VERSION_CHECK
     \li Do not warn when the SDK is newer than the newest tested version.
\row \li \c QT_FORCE_WARN_APPLE_SDK_AND_XCODE_CHECK
     \li Turn the error for an unsupported SDK or Xcode version into a
         warning.
\endtable

\sa qt_finalize_target()
*/
